  "id": "abstraction",
  "term": "abstraction",
  "definition": "Abstraction is the mental process of focusing attention on features of something that matter for a current purpose while recognizing and setting aside features that do not. In thought, it helps a person connect a part or quality of one experience with similar parts or qualities in other experiences, rather than staying with the whole original context.",
